# Learn Section Content

Browse Greek content organised by topic: conversations, phrases, nouns, verbs, and essentials.

## Route Structure

```
/learn                        Landing page: SectionIndex table of contents
/learn/conversations/:tab     Themed dialogues
/learn/phrases/:tab           Common expressions
/learn/nouns                  Everyday nouns, one card per subject
/learn/nouns/:subject         Nouns in one subject, filterable by CEFR level
/learn/verbs                  Verb inventory: irregulars to memorise vs verbs that follow the rules
/learn/verbs/:verbId          One verb's every form
/learn/essentials             Essentials landing (SectionIndex)
/learn/essentials/:subtab     Building blocks (numbers, colours, etc.)
/learn/tables/:tab            Lookup tables (see tables/content.llm)
```

## Landing Page

<route path="/learn">
<purpose>Section hub: a Greek-first table of contents for the learning content areas</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/index.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Rendered by the shared `SectionIndex` (`src/components/SectionIndex.tsx`): `PageHeading` "Learn" with lede "Browse Greek content by topic"
- Two groups, each a ruled list of rows; each row leads with the Greek name, then the English label and description:
  - Communication:
    - Διάλογοι / Conversations: "Real situations with family and friends" (links to /learn/conversations/arriving)
    - Φράσεις / Phrases: "Common expressions and useful phrases" (links to /learn/phrases/survival)
  - Words:
    - Ουσιαστικά / Nouns: "Objects, people, places — with gender" (links to /learn/nouns)
    - Ρήματα / Verbs: "The irregulars, then the verbs that follow the rules" (links to /learn/verbs)
    - Βασικά / Essentials: "Numbers, colours, time, position" (links to /learn/essentials)
    - Πίνακες / Tables: "Every form of the articles, nouns, pronouns, adjectives and verbs" (links to /learn/tables/articles)
</displays>
<note>
No cards, icons or tints. The group headings are plain stone text: a coloured slab beside the Doer and Owner colours would read as a grammatical claim (see the `SectionIndex` docblock).
</note>
</route>

## Subsections

See individual content files for detailed documentation:
- `conversations/content.llm` - Themed dialogues
- `phrases/content.llm` - Common expressions
- `essentials/content.llm` - Numbers, colours, time, position, frequency
- `tables/content.llm` - Lookup tables (was Reference); /learn/nouns and /learn/verbs link to them with "Every form, by family"

Nouns and verbs have no content file:
- `/learn/nouns` (`nouns/index.tsx`): `TabHero` "Everyday nouns", then an "Every form, by family" link to /learn/tables/nouns; one card per subject with its word count and three sample lemmas. Subjects come from `groupNounsBySubject` (`src/lib/noun-browser-groups.ts`) over `getNounsWithFormsAndSubjects()`.
- `/learn/nouns/$subject` (`nouns/$subject.tsx`): subject title, CEFR level toggles, nouns in subgroups via `NounList` (`learn/components/noun-list.tsx`). For an unknown subject the loader throws `notFound()`.
- `/learn/verbs` (`verbs/index.tsx`): `TabHero` "Verbs", an "Every form, by family" link to /learn/tables/verbs/present, then two tabs, "Irregulars (N)" (`MemoriseSection`) and "Follow the rules" (`RulesSection`), both from `verbs/components/verb-inventory.tsx`.
- `/learn/verbs/$verbId` (`verbs/$verbId.tsx`): one verb's forms through `TenseNavigator` ("Every form") and `ImperativeTable`, in plain words (one action / ongoing, simple past). A non-numeric or unknown id is a 404 (`notFound()`). Reached from search and from verb names in Learn → Tables.
